# Scenario 01 – Account Lockout and Password Reset

## Ticket Summary
A domain user became locked out after repeated failed sign-in attempts and required administrative intervention to restore access.

## Environment
- **Domain Controller:** Windows Server Active Directory
- **Client Machine:** Windows domain-joined VM
- **User Account:** testuser1
- **Ticket System:** osTicket with LDAP integration

## Objective
To simulate a common help desk scenario in which a user is locked out of their domain account and requires account unlock and password reset through Active Directory.

## Trigger Method
The issue was intentionally triggered by entering the wrong password multiple times at the Windows client login screen until the domain account lockout threshold was reached.

## Symptoms Observed
- User could not sign in to the client machine
- Repeated login failures led to account lockout
- A help desk ticket was created in osTicket to request assistance

## Ticket Workflow
- User account lockout occurred on domain-joined client
- Ticket was created in osTicket
- Technician reviewed the issue
- Account was unlocked and password reset in Active Directory
- Login was validated on the client machine
- Ticket was documented and closed

## Resolution Steps
1. Verified the user account in Active Directory Users and Computers
2. Confirmed the account was locked out
3. Unlocked the user account
4. Reset the password
5. Enabled "User must change password at next logon"
6. Returned to the client machine and signed in with the temporary password
7. Confirmed successful login and password update
8. Documented the resolution in osTicket and closed the ticket

## Validation
- User was able to sign in successfully after the account was unlocked
- Password change prompt appeared as expected
- Ticket was updated with resolution notes and marked closed

